            "description": "[confidence=high, sources=static] [from D3D11InstallHelper.dll] The malware string 'IsDebuggerPresent' was found in the binary. This string is characteristic of Debugger Evasion behavior. The presence of this specific string alone (no other Debugger Evasion-related string corroborates it) indicates the malware has capabilities associated with this technique, but with less certainty than a corroborated combination would. | [from D3D11InstallHelper.dll] The API functions UnhandledExceptionFilter, IsDebuggerPresent, SetUnhandledExceptionFilter are all imported by the binary. This combination is characteristic of Debugger Evasion \u2014 multiple corroborating APIs together, not one import in isolation, is what makes this a strong signal. | [from D3D11InstallHelper.dll] YARA rule 'AntiDebug_IsDebuggerPresent' matched the sample. This rule was specifically designed to detect Debugger Evasion patterns, confirming the presence of this capability. | [from 66VOAk0O.exe] The malware string 'IsDebuggerPresent' was found in the binary. This string is characteristic of Debugger Evasion behavior. The presence of this specific string alone (no other Debugger Evasion-related string corroborates it) indicates the malware has capabilities associated with this technique, but with less certainty than a corroborated combination would. | [from 66VOAk0O.exe] The API functions SetUnhandledExceptionFilter, UnhandledExceptionFilter, IsDebuggerPresent are all imported by the binary. This combination is characteristic of Debugger Evasion \u2014 multiple corroborating APIs together, not one import in isolation, is what makes this a strong signal. | [from 66VOAk0O.exe] YARA rule 'AntiDebug_IsDebuggerPresent' matched the sample. This rule was specifically designed to detect Debugger Evasion patterns, confirming the presence of this capability.",
